Sure — everything from the blue boxes except the Java code, with the original numbering/order.

1. Start a Hadoop container

PS> cd C:\bda-labs
PS> mkdir lab1-wordcount
PS> cd lab1-wordcount
PS> docker run -dit --name hadoop apache/hadoop:3.3.6 bash

2. Open a shell inside the container

PS> docker exec -it hadoop bash

Create the Java file

hadoop@a1b2c3:~$ nano WordCount.java

Paste the Java code from the lab manual, then save with Ctrl+O, Enter, and exit with Ctrl+X.

⸻

Execution & Expected Output

1. Create some input text

hadoop@a1b2c3:~$ mkdir input
hadoop@a1b2c3:~$ echo "the quick brown fox the lazy dog the fox" > input/file1.txt
hadoop@a1b2c3:~$ echo "a quick dog and a brown fox jumped" > input/file2.txt

2. Compile the program

hadoop@a1b2c3:~$ export HADOOP_CLASSPATH=$(hadoop classpath)
hadoop@a1b2c3:~$ mkdir classes
hadoop@a1b2c3:~$ javac -classpath $HADOOP_CLASSPATH -d classes WordCount.java
hadoop@a1b2c3:~$ jar -cvf wordcount.jar -C classes .

3. Run the job

hadoop@a1b2c3:~$ hadoop jar wordcount.jar WordCount input output

